0..49 Comment "// A record face is a named set of record labels."
50..52 Comment "//"
53..130 Comment "// A `where` block declares faces after a record type. A static bracket fixes"
131..208 Comment "// fields by label, by face or by a system of faces. In a system, the checker"
209..285 Comment "// converts the value of each later face with the value of the first face on"
286..300 Comment "// their meet."
301..303 Comment "//"
304..383 Comment "// The checker checks each fixed value at its field type. A patched value keeps"
384..460 Comment "// its free fields. A selection returns a fixed value. A record type ends at"
461..540 Comment "// `}` and keeps its labels as its boundary without a block. `|->` spells `↦`"
541..553 Comment "// in ASCII."
554..571 Comment "// - record label"
572..588 Comment "// - record face"
589..607 Comment "// - record system"
608..628 Comment "// - theory boundary"
629..645 Comment "// - lazy record"
646..657 Comment "// - codata"
658..660 Comment "//"
661..739 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/record-faces.gandr` — a face past the labels, a"
740..815 Comment "//   face named twice, a bracket naming a field or a face the type lacks, a"
816..887 Comment "//   literal stating a fixed field at another value, and two faces that"
888..924 Comment "//   disagree on their meet, refused"
925..1004 Comment "// - see: `model/desc/shaped-signature.gandr` — a theory\'s `boundary` and its"
1005..1015 Comment "//   faces"
1016..1087 Comment "// - owes: #6504 — a lazy record and a codata declaration hold faces."
